From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 22:51:13 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Crash resistance: tolerate torn journal prepare, reclaim
 orphaned blocks, add power-cut sweep

- journal: ignore/clear a COMMIT-less valid tail after a ring gap (torn BEGIN/UPDATE window); COMMIT after a gap still fails closed
- volume: OpenedVolume::reclaim_orphaned_blocks (ownership-checked), run by VolumeSession::open and recover-image
- volume: keep I/O errors from in-allocator journal recovery as I/O instead of Corrupt
- tests: crash_sweep (power cut at every write/flush, 4 cache-loss modes, 17 mutations x 2 block sizes), journal gap tests, orphan reclamation tests
- ci: run the exhaustive sweep in release; docs: P2 contract and recovery design
- clippy: drop needless drop of a closure
